  operational issue rule (D5): P(O >= 60) >= 0.10
  crowding threshold: 60 passengers (75 % of capacity 80)
  peak slots: (7, 8, 9, 17, 18, 19)
  bootstrap: 1000 resamples of complete replicas, seed 20261013
  equivalence: 95 % CI of the IA-AG difference inside +-margin -> EQUIVALENT;
               CI entirely outside -> NOT EQUIVALENT; otherwise INCONCLUSIVE


F1/F2 - IA vs AG and empirical fit by stratum group
---------------------------------------------------
Strata: direction x stop x departure slot (475). Groups come from config (peak slots), known_data (demand tertiles,
cuts on the empirical mean occupancy), route position, and the model INPUTS (BASE_DATA): boarding intensity = mean of
the input boarding distributions per stop (NORMAL: Param1; NEGATIVE BINOMIAL: r(1-p)/p; GEOMETRICAL rows ignored);
alighting intensity proxy = mean beta-binomial alpha/(alpha+beta) per stop. Terminal-adjacent = first two stops after the
departure terminal and last two before the final one.
