Largest |IA - AG| in the share of accepted strata over all 12 rules: 1.68 pp. The sign of the difference changes across rules; it is positive (IA ahead) for most rules and negative for a few, always below 2 pp.
Mean distance: IA is ahead of AG under every metric (last table above), by about 1 % of the error. Under every rule
both models accept the same share of strata within about 2 pp, and at the project rule (BC >= 0.97) both reject the majority (IA 37.9 % accepted, AG 36.2 %).

F4 - Input-calibration sensitivity
----------------------------------
NOT done. It needs new simulations with perturbed input distributions; the 1000 replicas of each run share one
set of fitted parameters, so their variability is not uncertainty in the calibration (plan 14).

F5 - External validity
----------------------
Demonstrated: one route (line 401, 12 buses, 82 + 81 trips), working days only, one demand regime, validation against
fitted normals of the same operational period that calibrated the inputs (calibration-period, not out-of-sample).
Hypotheses, not findings: other routes, holidays or free-travel days, atypical demand, changed frequency or capacity.
